<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101589" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαιρ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make into a globule</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάπυρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aphr.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1.93
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be rounded</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				7.9.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στήθεα δ᾽
			ἐσφαίρωτο</span> his chest <i>was round and arched</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be curled up in a ball</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴ -ωθεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					3.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, metaph., <i>to be concentrated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				400
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in 
				Pass.
			 also of blunted weapons, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσφαιρωμένα ἀκόντια</span> spears <i>with buttons</i>
			at the point, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				8.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γρόσφοι -ωμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.20.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιδήρια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					71.29
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λελογχωμένον δόρυ</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1111a12
			</span></i>.</div>
